  "title": "ERP CORE",
  "description": "ERP CORE (Compendium of Open Resources and Experiments) is an open resource of raw EEG recordings from 40 neurotypical adults performing six optimized task paradigms. The paradigms elicit seven widely used ERP components: N170, MMN, N2pc, N400, P3, LRP and ERN. The dataset includes event code schemes, task stimuli for the N170, MMN and N400 paradigms, and participant demographics.",
  "methods_description": "Each participant completed six tasks in randomized order: Eriksen flanker, passive auditory oddball, face perception, visual search, word pair judgment and active visual oddball. Task parameters were counterbalanced within participants where possible. Interstimulus intervals were jittered to prevent phase-locking of alpha-band oscillations. Rest breaks were participant-controlled between blocks.",
